1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,503
Verana.

2
00:00:00,503 --> 00:00:04,670
The open trust infrastructure for the verifiable internet.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,695
First, the foundations.

4
00:00:07,695 --> 00:00:11,085
Verifiable credentials are becoming a reality.

5
00:00:11,085 --> 00:00:16,170
The groundwork is laid: issuer, holder, verifier, one trust triangle.

6
00:00:16,170 --> 00:00:25,160
And implementations are arriving in every sector: each ecosystem potentially bringing value to the entire digital economy.

7
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,816
Let's have a look at the challenges of interconnecting ecosystems.

8
00:00:31,816 --> 00:00:36,574
One: create new ecosystems at will, and monetize them.

9
00:00:36,574 --> 00:00:38,865
Two: scale across borders.

10
00:00:38,865 --> 00:00:41,420
Three: authenticate mutually.

11
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:46,090
And four: discovery: find trusted services, anywhere.

12
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:51,272
Let's dig into challenge one: scale, by creating ecosystems.

13
00:00:51,272 --> 00:01:04,800
How do we create new trust registries at will: publish schemas and accreditation lists, define business models, and make each ecosystem publicly discoverable, interconnectable, and joinable?

14
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:08,389
Next, challenge two: scale, cross-border.

15
00:01:08,389 --> 00:01:14,670
How do we recognize and onboard ecosystems from any country, and any sector?

16
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:18,327
Then, challenge three: mutual authentication.

17
00:01:18,327 --> 00:01:25,500
How do services and AI agents from different countries identify each other, and trust each other?

18
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,057
And finally, challenge four: discovery.

19
00:01:29,057 --> 00:01:32,740
How do we search the graph of trusted services?

20
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,226
The good news?

21
00:01:34,226 --> 00:01:36,590
Verana answers all of this.

22
00:01:36,590 --> 00:01:42,370
Sovereign ecosystems, verifiable services, one public Trust Graph.

23
00:01:42,370 --> 00:01:46,310
Open, neutral, cross-border, owned by no one.

24
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,005
So let's build.

25
00:01:48,005 --> 00:01:53,636
Setting up your own sovereign ecosystem trust registry in Verana is straightforward.

26
00:01:53,636 --> 00:02:02,215
Start by creating your trust registry, publish your Ecosystem Governance Framework, your credential schemas and business models.

27
00:02:02,215 --> 00:02:04,628
Onboard your ecosystem participants.

28
00:02:04,628 --> 00:02:07,510
Your ecosystem exists, and is discoverable.

29
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:10,985
Then deploy your services and AI agents.

30
00:02:10,985 --> 00:02:13,075
Choose your business wallet.

31
00:02:13,075 --> 00:02:16,881
Join ecosystems, on Verana or on other trust lists.

32
00:02:16,881 --> 00:02:23,000
Attach their credentials to your services: you are now visible in the Trust Graph.

33
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:30,090
And issue and verify credentials, to personal wallets, AI agents, or any service with a wallet.

34
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,768
And here is the result.

35
00:02:32,768 --> 00:02:35,534
You are now part of the Trust Graph.

36
00:02:35,534 --> 00:02:43,988
Any person, service, or AI agent can find you, mutually authenticate with verifiable credentials, and connect.

37
00:02:43,988 --> 00:02:47,370
Trust, established before the first message.

38
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:49,136
One more thing.

39
00:02:49,136 --> 00:02:54,591
Behind Verana: open specifications, built exclusively on open standards.

40
00:02:54,591 --> 00:02:56,182
Open-source software.

41
00:02:56,182 --> 00:03:00,273
And a non-profit foundation, managed by its community.

42
00:03:00,273 --> 00:03:01,712
Want to contribute?

43
00:03:01,712 --> 00:03:05,424
Join the Foundation: it is free for contributors.

44
00:03:05,424 --> 00:03:08,530
Join a working group, or create your own.

45
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,540
In essence: Verana enables trust to scale.

46
00:03:12,540 --> 00:03:18,018
Not just within one ecosystem: across the entire digital economy.

47
00:03:18,018 --> 00:03:21,558
Try it yourself, on the public playground.

48
00:03:21,558 --> 00:03:22,738
Verana dot io.

